<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Rotula</displayName>
  <description>Settings for the Rotula label designer.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Rotula_0_4">Rotula 0.4.0 or later</string>
      <string id="Cat_P4Software">P4 Software</string>
      <string id="Cat_Rotula">Rotula</string>

      <string id="Language">Language of Rotula</string>
      <string id="Language_Explain">Sets the language of Rotula and locks it: View &gt; Language is disabled and says "Managed by your organization".

"Same as Windows" uses Spanish when the Windows display language is Spanish and English otherwise.

Not configured or disabled: each user chooses the language.

Registry value: Language (text: auto, en or es).</string>
      <string id="Language_Auto">Same as Windows</string>
      <string id="Language_En">English</string>
      <string id="Language_Es">Spanish</string>

      <string id="UpdateCheck">Check for updates</string>
      <string id="UpdateCheck_Explain">Controls the daily update check and locks the choice (Help &gt; Check for updates once a day).

Enabled: once a day Rotula asks the public GitHub page of the project which version is the newest, with one anonymous request. Nothing about the user or the computer is sent. When a newer version exists, a notice with a link to the release page appears. Rotula never downloads or installs anything itself.

Disabled: Rotula makes no update request at all, and users cannot switch it on.

Not configured: each user decides. The check is off until the user switches it on.

Registry value: UpdateCheck (number: 1 on, 0 off).</string>

      <string id="DefaultPrinter">Default printer</string>
      <string id="DefaultPrinter_Explain">Preselects this Windows printer in the Print dialog for users who have not chosen a printer yet. Users can still choose another printer; their choice is remembered.

Type the printer name exactly as Windows shows it. If the printer is not installed on the computer, Rotula falls back to the Windows default printer without a message.

Registry value: DefaultPrinter (text).</string>

      <string id="UserAddOns">Allow data source add-ons from the user's folder</string>
      <string id="UserAddOns_Explain">Data source add-ons are programs. Rotula loads add-ons from the "packs" folder next to the program (installed by an administrator) and, after the user approves each one, from %AppData%\Rotula\packs.

Disabled: add-ons in the user's folder are not loaded and not offered for approval. Add-ons in the installed "packs" folder still work.

Enabled or not configured: users may approve add-ons in their own folder.

Registry value: UserAddOns (number: 0 blocks the user's folder).</string>

      <string id="McpPrinting">Allow the MCP server to print</string>
      <string id="McpPrinting_Explain">The Rotula MCP server (Rotula.Mcp.exe) lets an AI assistant design labels. Printing is off unless its settings file allows it.

Disabled: the MCP server never prints, whatever its settings file says.

Enabled or not configured: the settings file of the MCP server decides (allowPrinting and allowedPrinters). This policy cannot switch printing on by itself.

Registry value: McpPrinting (number: 0 blocks).</string>

      <string id="McpDatabase">Allow the MCP server to read databases</string>
      <string id="McpDatabase_Explain">Disabled: the Rotula MCP server never reads saved database connections, whatever its settings file says.

Enabled or not configured: the settings file of the MCP server decides (allowDatabase). This policy cannot switch database access on by itself.

Registry value: McpDatabase (number: 0 blocks).</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="Language">
        <dropdownList refId="Language" defaultItem="0">Language:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="DefaultPrinter">
        <textBox refId="DefaultPrinter">
          <label>Printer name:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
